\section{The Session Gap}\label{sec:gap}

Let $a_4$ be the accuracy of a model trained on sessions 1--3 and tested on session 4,
and $a_5$ that of the same model trained on sessions 1--4 and tested on session 5; we call
$g=a_4-a_5$ the \emph{session gap}. If a feature block was fitted to the labels of
sessions 1--4, a model reading it will score higher on session 4 than on session 5, and
a large positive $g$ will appear only in blocks fitted to those labels. The two sides of
the comparison also differ in the number of training sessions, three for $a_4$ and four
for $a_5$; a matched design at the end of this section removes that difference.

