\textbf{Usage survey.} The audit is purposive: starting from papers that cite MMGCN or
DialogueGCN and the code they link, we inspected the code, and where available the paper,
of twenty MERC systems published since MMGCN, and recorded which feature file and block
the data loader reads and which split the evaluation uses. Five load the shared text
block: MM-DFN, GraphCFC, GraphMFT, GA2MIF and
DialogueCRN~\cite{hu2022mmdfn,li2023graphcfc,li2023graphmft,li2023ga2mif,hu2021dialoguecrn}
(the last ships the DialogueGCN file with its code, byte-identical by MD5). Three pair
their own text encoder with the audio and visual blocks of the bc-LSTM file, the
combination of the fusion experiment in Section~\ref{sec:conseq}, and seven pair it with
MMGCN's audio and visual blocks. Two use other features or blocks whose source the release
does not show, and three have no code release. All eight systems that load released
bc-LSTM blocks test on the file's session-5 split. We found no published result that
cross-validates on these files; the cross-validated study in~\cite{poria2018baselines}
does not state whether it used them. In this sample the leak is a latent hazard. A group
that follows the recommendation to cross-validate~\cite{antoniou2023} on these files
would be exposed to it, and the stress test of Section~\ref{sec:loso} indicates its size
for one of the five systems. Table~\ref{tab:usage} summarises the audit; the per-system
evidence (repository URL, commit, file path and code line) is in the accompanying
repository.

