\textbf{Effect on rankings.} A leak that added the same constant to every system would
leave comparisons intact; here the ranking changes (Fig.~\ref{fig:rank}). Ranking the
eleven configurations of Table~\ref{tab:loso} by their LOSO mean and by their
standard-split accuracy gives Kendall's $\tau=0.35$ ($p=0.17$). The three configurations
with the shared text block take the top three places under LOSO and places 4, 6 and 7 on
the standard split, while the three leading standard-split configurations, all built on
frozen encoders, fall to places 4 to 6. Among our eleven tested configurations, a
comparison of feature sets under LOSO does reach the opposite conclusion from one on the
standard split. The rank correlation itself is not significant with eleven
configurations, so the result concerns which kind of configuration leads under each
protocol.

